From b59ea7e99bb27569321ce474ccb81206cf8ad0c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:10:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/timer: TC model, checked against PIC32CM MC00 silicon

mchp-tc (U2249): COUNT8/16/32 counting from GCLK_TC through the
prescaler, up or down, TOP per WAVE.WAVEGEN (PER, MAX or CC0), overflow
and compare-match flags with the interrupt, one-shot, the RETRIGGER,
STOP, UPDATE and READSYNC commands, double buffering, COUNT32 pairing
(STATUS.SLAVE on the odd TC; the SoC links TC0/TC1, TC2/TC3). COUNT
reads return the last synchronized value. Event-driven on the virtual
clock; the timer only runs while an event changes something.

Behaviour the data sheet leaves open follows silicon (test images
tests/tcprobe.c and tests/tc.c, transcripts byte-identical to the
twin's): counting starts from COUNT in either direction, starting is an
UPDATE condition, PER/CCx reads show the buffers while PERBUFV/CCBUFVx
are set while TOP and the compare values keep the old values,
synchronized writes without GCLK_TC keep SYNCBUSY set.

mchp-regblock gains a gclk_update class hook (pre- and post-update) for
models that time from their GCLK channel. New qtest pic32cm-tc-test.

Peripheral Pretender downstream patch; not for upstream submission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
